.TH SDL_ShowNotificationWithProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ShowNotificationWithProperties \- Show a system notification.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_notification.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_NotificationID SDL_ShowNotificationWithProperties(SDL_PropertiesID props);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
System notifications are small, asynchronous popup windows that notify the user of some information\[char46] How they are displayed is system dependent\[char46]
.PP
These are the supported properties:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_TITLE_STRING :
the title of the notification, in UTF-8 encoding\[char46] This property is required\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_ACTIONS_POINTER :
An array of pointers to
.BR SDL_NotificationAction
structs that will add actions to the notification, usually in the form of buttons or menu items\[char46] Note that systems may have a limit on the maximum number of actions that a notification can have\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATIONS_ACTION_COUNT_NUMBER :
the number of actions in the array of actions, if it exists\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_IMAGE_POINTER :
a pointer to an
.BR SDL_Surface
containing an image that will be attached to the notification\[char46] In most cases, the image is displayed in the form of a large icon or thumbnail alongside the message body\[char46] Notifications on Apple platforms can be expanded to show a larger format image\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_MESSAGE_STRING :
the message body of the notification, in UTF-8 encoding\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_PRIORITY_NUMBER :
an
.BR SDL_NotificationPriority
value representing the notification priority\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_REPLACES_NUMBER :
the
.BR SDL_NotificationID
of a previously shown notification that this notification should replace\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_SOUND_STRING :
sets a sound to play when the notification is shown\[char46] This can have the value \(dqdefault\(dq, to play the system default notification sound, \(dqsilent\(dq, to play no sound, or contain the path to a file with a custom sound\[char46] The paths and formats that can be used for custom sounds are system-specific, and can have some restrictions, depending on the platform:
.PP
\(bu Apple platforms require that the sound file is contained within the app bundle\[char46] Supported formats are: Linear PCM, MA4 (IMA/ADPCM), uLaw, or aLaw, in an \[char46]aiff, \[char46]wav, or \[char46]caf file\[char46]
.PP
\(bu Windows can only play custom notification sounds when the app is packaged inside an MSIX installer\[char46] Playback from arbitrary file paths is not supported\[char46] Supported formats are: \[char46]aac, \[char46]flac, \[char46]m4a, \[char46]mp3, \[char46]wav, and \[char46]wma\[char46]
.PP
\(bu Unix platforms can generally load sounds from any arbitrary path, as long as the read permissions are correct\[char46] Supported formats are: ogg/opus, ogg/vorbis, and wav/pcm\[char46] If this property is not set, the system default sound will be used\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_NOTIFICATION_TRANSIENT_BOOLEAN :
true if the notification should not persist in the system notification center after initially being shown\[char46]
.PP
Not all properties are supported by all platforms\[char46]
.PP
Notifications are available on: - Windows 10 or higher - macOS 10\[char46]14 or higher - iOS 11 or higher - *nix platforms that support the org\[char46]freedesktop\[char46]Notifications, or org\[char46]freedesktop\[char46]portal\[char46]Notification interfaces

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I props
the properties to be used when creating this notification\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns A non-zero
.BR SDL_NotificationID
on success or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_ShowNotification (3),
.BR SDL_NotificationAction (3type),
.BR SDL_NotificationPriority (3),
.BR SDL_NotificationEvent (3type)
